    "# Neural Networks Fundamentals\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook covers the fundamental concepts of neural networks that form the building blocks for our CNN-based magnetic field prediction models.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Learning Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "After completing this notebook, you will understand:\n",
    "- The basic architecture of artificial neural networks\n",
    "- How neurons and layers work together\n",
    "- The role of activation functions\n",
    "- Loss functions and optimization concepts\n",
    "- Backpropagation algorithm basics\n",
    "- Implementation of a simple neural network for field prediction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Neural Network Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "Neural Networks consist of collections of neurons that are connected in an acyclic graph. The outputs of neurons in a fully connected layer can become inputs to other neurons through pairwise connections.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Characteristics:\n",
    "- **Acyclic Graph**: No cycles are allowed to prevent infinite loops during forward pass\n",
    "- **Layered Structure**: Neurons in the same layer don't share connections\n",
    "- **Weight Sharing**: Connections have learnable weights\n",
    "- **Hierarchical Processing**: Information flows from input to output through layers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.patches as patches\n",
    "from matplotlib.patches import Circle, FancyBboxPatch, ConnectionPatch\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import make_regression\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set up plotting style\n",
    "plt.style.use('default')\n",
    "sns.set_palette(\"husl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def draw_neural_network(ax, layers, title=\"Neural Network Architecture\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Draw a neural network architecture diagram.\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    n_layers = len(layers)\n",
    "    max_neurons = max(layers)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Calculate positions\n",
    "    layer_spacing = 3\n",
    "    neuron_spacing = 1.5\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Draw neurons and connections\n",
    "    for i, n_neurons in enumerate(layers):\n",
    "        x = i * layer_spacing\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Position neurons\n",
    "        if n_neurons == 1:\n",
    "            y_positions = [0]\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            y_start = -(n_neurons - 1) * neuron_spacing / 2\n",
    "            y_positions = [y_start + j * neuron_spacing for j in range(n_neurons)]\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Draw connections to next layer\n",
    "        if i < n_layers - 1:\n",
    "            next_n_neurons = layers[i + 1]\n",
    "            if next_n_neurons == 1:\n",
    "                next_y_positions = [0]\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                next_y_start = -(next_n_neurons - 1) * neuron_spacing / 2\n",
    "                next_y_positions = [next_y_start + j * neuron_spacing for j in range(next_n_neurons)]\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Draw connections\n",
    "            for y1 in y_positions:\n",
    "                for y2 in next_y_positions:\n",
    "                    alpha = 0.3 if (n_neurons > 5 and next_n_neurons > 5) else 0.5\n",
    "                    ax.plot([x, x + layer_spacing], [y1, y2], \n",
    "                           'gray', alpha=alpha, linewidth=0.5, zorder=1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Draw neurons\n",
    "        for j, y in enumerate(y_positions):\n",
    "            # Different colors for different layers\n",
    "            if i == 0:\n",
    "                color = '#4ECDC4'  # Input layer\n",
    "                size = 0.4\n",
    "            elif i == n_layers - 1:\n",
    "                color = '#FF6B6B'  # Output layer\n",
    "                size = 0.4\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                color = '#45B7D1'  # Hidden layers\n",
    "                size = 0.35\n",
    "            \n",
    "            circle = Circle((x, y), size, color=color, alpha=0.8, zorder=3)\n",
    "            ax.add_patch(circle)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Add layer labels\n",
    "            if j == len(y_positions) // 2:\n",
    "                if i == 0:\n",
    "                    label = 'Input\\nLayer'\n",
    "                elif i == n_layers - 1:\n",
    "                    label = 'Output\\nLayer'\n",
    "                else:\n",
    "                    label = f'Hidden\\nLayer {i}'\n",
    "                \n",
    "                ax.text(x, y - 1.2, label, ha='center', va='center', \n",
    "                       fontsize=9, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Set plot properties\n",
    "    ax.set_xlim(-1, (n_layers - 1) * layer_spacing + 1)\n",
    "    max_y = max_neurons * neuron_spacing / 2 + 2\n",
    "    ax.set_ylim(-max_y, max_y)\n",
    "    ax.set_aspect('equal')\n",
    "    ax.axis('off')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', pad=20)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Draw example neural network architectures\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 8))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Simple network\n",
    "draw_neural_network(axes[0], [3, 5, 1], \n",
    "                 \"Simple Neural Network\\n(1 Hidden Layer)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Deep network\n",
    "draw_neural_network(axes[1], [3, 8, 6, 4, 1], \n",
    "                 \"Deep Neural Network\\n(3 Hidden Layers)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Key Observations:\")\n",
    "print(\"- Input layer receives the raw features (geometry, material, excitation)\")\n",
    "print(\"- Hidden layers perform feature transformation and extraction\")\n",
    "print(\"- Output layer produces the magnetic field prediction\")\n",
    "print(\"- Connections between layers have learnable weights\")"
   ]
